---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import logo from '../assets/estrogen.png';

const NPM = 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sysce/estrogen';
const JS_OBF = 'https://github.com/javascript-obfuscator/javascript-obfuscator';
---

<Base>
	<main class="container">
		<header class="masthead">
			<div class="brand">
				<Image src={logo} alt="estrogen" width={56} height={56} />
				<div>
					<h1>estrogen</h1>
					<span class="ver" id="engineVersion">loading engine...</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<a class="npm-btn" href={NPM} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				<svg
					class="npm-mark"
					width="36"
					height="15"
					viewBox="0 0 36 15"
					aria-hidden="true"
				>
					<rect width="36" height="15" rx="2.5" fill="#fff"></rect>
					<text
						x="18"
						y="11.4"
						text-anchor="middle"
						font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"
						font-weight="700"
						font-size="10"
						fill="#cb3837">npm</text
					>
				</svg>
				<span>@sysce/estrogen</span>
			</a>
		</header>

		<p class="lede">
			Want to protect your site from crawlers? estrogen transforms your built
			JavaScript into something more fun. Drop in a file or a whole codebase and
			it rewrites the strings and shortens the names,
			<strong>right in your browser</strong>. Nothing you load leaves your
			machine, and it comes back ready to ship. This page is a web UI in the
			spirit of <a href={JS_OBF}>javascript-obfuscator</a> and obfuscator.io,
			running the real estrogen engine compiled to WebAssembly.
		</p>

		<section class="panel" id="app">
			<div class="tabs" role="tablist">
				<button class="tab active" type="button" data-tab="code" role="tab"
					>Copy &amp; paste JavaScript</button
				>
				<button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="upload" role="tab"
					>Upload a folder</button
				>
				<button class="tab" type="button" data-tab="output" role="tab"
					>Output</button
				>
			</div>

			<div class="pane active" data-pane="code">
				<div class="editor-wrap">
					<textarea id="editor"></textarea>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="pane" data-pane="upload">
				<div class="dropzone" id="dropZone">
					<svg
						class="dz-icon"
						viewBox="0 0 24 24"
						fill="none"
						stroke="currentColor"
						stroke-width="1.6"
						stroke-linecap="round"
						stroke-linejoin="round"
						aria-hidden="true"
					>
						<path
							d="M12 16V4m0 0 4 4m-4-4-4 4M4 16v2a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-2"
						></path>
					</svg>
					<span class="big">Pick a folder, or drop files here</span>
					<span class="sub"
						>estrogen runs on every .js, .mjs and .cjs file in the folder. Every
						other file is copied through unchanged. You get the whole tree back
						as a .zip. Nothing leaves your browser.</span
					>
				</div>
				<input
					type="file"
					id="folderInput"
					webkitdirectory
					multiple
					hidden
				/>
				<div class="upload-status" id="uploadStatus">
					<div class="progress-track">
						<div class="progress-fill" id="progressFill"></div>
					</div>
					<div class="progress-text" id="progressText"></div>
					<div class="skips" id="skips"></div>
					<div>
						<button class="btn btn-primary" id="downloadZipBtn" disabled
							>Download .zip</button
						>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="pane" data-pane="output">
				<div class="output-wrap">
					<button class="copy-btn" id="copyBtn" type="button">Copy</button>
					<textarea id="output" readonly spellcheck="false"></textarea>
				</div>
				<div class="output-meta">
					<span id="editsCount"></span>
					<button class="btn" id="downloadBtn" disabled type="button"
						>Download .js</button
					>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="toolbar">
				<div class="opt">
					<label for="seed">Seed</label>
					<input
						class="input"
						type="text"
						id="seed"
						placeholder="empty = random keys each run"
					/>
				</div>
				<span class="engine" id="engineNote"></span>
				<button class="btn" id="resetBtn" type="button">Reset</button>
				<button class="btn btn-primary" id="obfuscateBtn" type="button"
					>Obfuscate</button
				>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="faq">
			<h2>FAQ</h2>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h3>Why would I obfuscate my JavaScript?</h3>
				<p>
					To make a shipped build more fun to read, for crawlers, scrapers and
					the casual copy/paste. estrogen takes the plain string and template
					literals out of the source and stores them in an encrypted pool, so a
					reader can no longer grep for a message, a URL or a key name and land
					on the line that uses it.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h3>Is this foolproof?</h3>
				<p>
					No. The browser has to run the code, so a reader with time and patience
					can work it back. estrogen makes that a lot more work, which is the
					point.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h3>Why is the output larger than my source?</h3>
				<p>
					Because the pass prepends a decoder and stores the literals as an
					encrypted, base64 pool, which is bigger than the plain text it
					replaced. There is a lot of repetition in the decoder, so the output
					compresses well with gzip or brotli, which most servers already send.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h3>Does it work on any JavaScript?</h3>
				<p>
					It works on standard JavaScript and Node source that parses, including
					.mjs and .cjs. The browser demo runs one source string at a time through
					the pass, or every .js, .mjs and .cjs file when you upload a folder. If
					an input has no poolable string or template literal, the pass reports
					zero edits and the output matches the input. A file that fails to parse
					is copied through unchanged and noted as skipped.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h3>Is my code uploaded anywhere?</h3>
				<p>
					No. There is no server. The engine is WebAssembly running in this page,
					so your source never leaves your browser. Reload the tab and it is gone.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h3>Can I run it on my own machine?</h3>
				<p>
					Yes. estrogen is a post-build obfuscator published to npm as
					<code class="lit">@sysce/estrogen</code>. It rewrites an already-built
					output directory and has an Astro integration for build-time use. This
					page is the same engine compiled to WebAssembly.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>

	<script>
		import '../scripts/app.ts';
	</script>
</Base>
